ps://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-14T09:35:08Z","updated_at":"2026-08-14T09:35:08Z","body":"@stuartcarnie I've been looking into Metal for this and it seems most objects are queued for deletion when presenting, so this PR would not have benefit on it. Should this code path be simply disabled for Metal for the time being?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5291791122/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5309634247","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116540#issuecomment-5309634247","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116540","id":5309634247,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPHqWxw","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-16T20:57:47Z","updated_at":"2026-08-16T20:57:47Z","body":"@blueskythlikesclouds can you clarify\r\n\r\n> most object are queued for deletion when presenting\r\n\r\nI'm not sure what you mean by that.\r\n\r\nMost objects are managed via reference counting in Metal, so they are freed when the last reference is released. I _suspect_ it will become more interesting when I switch to placement heaps in #121392, as every object will typically have a single owner, meaning they'll be released deterministically.\r\n\r\nPerhaps we disable for now, and I revisit after #121392?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5309634247/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5309932885","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116540#issuecomment-5309932885","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116540","id":5309932885,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPH8lVQ","user":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-16T22:12:33Z","updated_at":"2026-08-16T22:12:33Z","body":"I meant `_untrack_resource`, which adds the resource to a pending residency deletion list, which gets handled in `_execute_and_present_barriers`. Does that not cause the resource to live until the command buffer execution, preventing the resource from being freed asynchronously?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5309932885/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5309946390","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116540#issuecomment-5309946390","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116540","id":5309946390,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPH9aFg","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-16T22:16:11Z","updated_at":"2026-08-16T22:16:11Z","body":"Yes, correct, @blueskythlikesclouds – that is gone from #121392. Tracking residency isn't used for Hazard tracking anyhow, but it is much cleaner in this new work.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5309946390/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5602648550","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116540#issuecomment-5602648550","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116540","id":5602648550,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTfGh5g","user":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-09T13:28:07Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T13:33:53Z","body":"I've been working more on this but I'm not convinced anymore that this is the way to do it. A lot of free operations are so cheap that spawning the task usually takes longer.\r\n\r\nIdeally, we want to asynchronously free when _actual_ GPU device memory gets freed. There isn't really a way to know when that happens by default in D3D12MA/VMA. It may either only delete the placed resource which is usually very cheap to do, or also delete the backing memory block which can potentially take several milliseconds. I figure we would need to modify them to report when the latter is going to happen.\r\n\r\nThe MRP I tested this on was a special case where it constantly kept allocating and freeing backing memory blocks, so for games out there I'm not sure whether the current implementation would bring benefit.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5602648550/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]